  "difficulty": 4,
  "marks": 8,
  "estimatedSeconds": 720,
  "stem": "A closed box is a cuboid with a square base of side $x$ cm and height $h$ cm. Its total surface area is 150 cm².",
  "parts": [
   {
    "label": "(a)",
    "type": "EXTENDED_RESPONSE",
    "marks": 3,
    "markingMode": "MANUAL",
    "stem": "Show that the volume of the box is $V = \\dfrac{75x - x^3}{2}$.",
    "answerSpec": {
     "markScheme": {
      "points": [
       {
        "id": "p1",
        "description": "M1 writes $2x^2 + 4xh = 150$.",
        "marks": 1
       },
       {
        "id": "p2",
        "description": "M1 rearranges: $h = \\frac{150 - 2x^2}{4x}$.",
        "marks": 1
       },
       {
        "id": "p3",
        "description": "A1 substitutes into $V = x^2h$ to reach the given result.",
        "marks": 1
       }
      ]
     },
     "modelAnswer": "$$\n2x^2 + 4xh = 150 \\Rightarrow h = \\frac{150 - 2x^2}{4x}\n$$\n\n$$\nV = x^2 h = \\frac{x(150 - 2x^2)}{4} = \\frac{150x - 2x^3}{4} = \\frac{75x - x^3}{2}\n$$"
    },
    "explanation": "Two square faces and four rectangular faces."
   },
   {
    "label": "(b)",
    "type": "NUMERICAL",
    "marks": 2,
    "stem": "Find the value of x for which V is stationary.",
    "payload": {
     "answerPrefix": "x ="
    },
    "answerSpec": {
     "value": 5
    },
    "explanation": "$\\frac{dV}{dx} = \\frac{75 - 3x^2}{2} = 0$ gives $x^2 = 25$, $x = 5$ ($x > 0$).",
    "workedSolution": "1. $\\frac{dV}{dx} = \\frac{75 - 3x^2}{2} = 0$ gives $x^2 = 25$, $x = 5$ ($x > 0$)."
   },
   {
    "label": "(c)",
    "type": "NUMERICAL",
    "marks": 2,
    "stem": "Find the value of $\\dfrac{d^2V}{dx^2}$ at this value of $x$, and hence show that $V$ is a maximum.",
    "answerSpec": {
     "value": -15
    },
    "explanation": "$\\frac{d^2V}{dx^2} = -3x = -15 < 0$, so a maximum.",
    "workedSolution": "1. $\\frac{d^2V}{dx^2} = -3x = -15 < 0$, so a maximum."
   },
   {
    "label": "(d)",
    "type": "NUMERICAL",
